{"name":"Rossini Red","hex":"#c4091e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gioachino Rossini","blocks":[{"text":"Gioachino Antonio Rossini was an Italian composer and conductor of the late Classical and early Romantic eras. While he gained most of his fame for his 39 operas, he also wrote many pieces of chamber music, piano, and some sacred music. He set new standards for both comic and serious opera before retiring from large-scale composition while still in his thirties, at the height of his popularity."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/Rossini_young-circa-1815.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gioachino_Rossini"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Giuseppe_Rossini_%28father_of_Gioachino_Rossini%29.jpg/500px-Giuseppe_Rossini_%28father_of_Gioachino_Rossini%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Giuseppe_Rossini_%28father_of_Gioachino_Rossini%29.jpg/500px-Giuseppe_Rossini_%28father_of_Gioachino_Rossini%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiuseppe_Rossini_(father_of_Gioachino_Rossini).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Anna_Rossini_%28mother_of_Gioachino_Rossini%29.jpg/500px-Anna_Rossini_%28mother_of_Gioachino_Rossini%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Anna_Rossini_%28mother_of_Gioachino_Rossini%29.jpg/500px-Anna_Rossini_%28mother_of_Gioachino_Rossini%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnna_Rossini_(mother_of_Gioachino_Rossini).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Alexandre_Fragonard_-_Sc%C3%A8ne_de_L%27orage_%28Barbier_de_S%C3%A9ville%29.jpg/500px-Alexandre_Fragonard_-_Sc%C3%A8ne_de_L%27orage_%28Barbier_de_S%C3%A9ville%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Alexandre_Fragonard_-_Sc%C3%A8ne_de_L%27orage_%28Barbier_de_S%C3%A9ville%29.jpg/1280px-Alexandre_Fragonard_-_Sc%C3%A8ne_de_L%27orage_%28Barbier_de_S%C3%A9ville%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Alexandre_Frag